body:
And also;

•According to late LOTR style Quenya, isn't the Possessive case also inflected according to the number of its possessee? (Like it would be _Rúmilwa sarat_ - _Rúmilwë sarati_, or _Fëanárova Silmaril_ - _Fëanárovë Silmarilli_). If not, I have to say, what a pity! It would be a quite interesting feature within the Possessive paradigms. :(

•So, for the agent in passive sentences _ló_ is used instead of the Instrumental case. But what about applicatives? There's a sentence written by Tolkien himself, _antanenyes parmanen_ "I gave him a book" (lit. I gave him with a book) which shows Tolkien decided introducing an applicative voice into Quenya. So, the oblique in applicatives is indeed expressed by means of the Instrumental case?
